law.text:
		A clinic or instructor license may be denied, suspended, or revoked on any one or more of the following grounds:

Material misstatement or omission in an application for a driver improvement clinic license or a driver improvement clinic instructor license;


Failure to comply subsequent to receipt of a written warning from the Department for any willful failure to comply with any provision of this chapter or any regulation promulgated by the Commissioner under this chapter; or any criteria established by the Department pursuant to this chapter;


Defrauding any student in a driver improvement clinic, or any other person in the conduct of a driver improvement clinic's business;


Employment of fraudulent devices, methods or practices in connection with compliance with the requirements under the statutes of the Commonwealth;


Having used deceptive acts or practices;


Knowingly advertising by any means any assertion, representation, or statement of fact which is untrue, misleading, or deceptive in any particular relating to the conduct of a clinic;


Having been convicted of any fraudulent act in connection with a driver improvement clinic or driver training school, or any consumer-related fraud;


Having been convicted of any criminal act involving the operation of a driver improvement clinic or driver training school;


Having been convicted of a felony;


Failing or refusing to pay civil penalties imposed by the Department pursuant to § 46.2-490.6.
